WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.570
We're The Office ladies.

8
00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:24.550
Hello.

9
00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:27.890
Happy finale part two.

10
00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:29.910
This is really it.

11
00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:36.430
This is season nine, episode 27, written by Greg Daniels, directed by Ken Kwapis.

12
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:38.650
Would you like a summary?

13
00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:39.750
I would.

14
00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:41.070
All right.

15
00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:45.250
Dwight and Angela are getting married.

16
00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:48.690
Kelly and Ryan are going to reunite.

17
00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.150
Nellie gets the baby she's been hoping for.

18
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.630
Pam and Jim make a very big decision about their future.

19
00:00:56.510 --> 00:01:00.750
And everyone at Dunder Mifflin gathers for one last night together.

20
00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:05.970
And this, you guys, remember when Greg asked us all what we hoped for our characters?

21
00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:10.450
Mine was, I hoped that Angela and Dwight would end up together.

22
00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.370
So I love watching this.

23
00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:14.270
It's so awesome.

24
00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:15.710
It's so perfect.

25
00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:20.130
Well, fast fact number one, Angela, is your look back moment.

26
00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:20.750
All right.

27
00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.190
This is our final look back.

28
00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:25.610
You know, this is the bonus feature on disc four for season nine.

29
00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:27.890
And when I was watching all of it,

30
00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:38.130
one of the things that really stood out to me was when everyone reflected on what the writers meant to the show and what Greg Daniels meant to everyone.

31
00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.350
Let's listen.

32
00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:42.190
First and foremost, it's a writer's show.

33
00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:46.350
And we really owe everything to the writers on this.

34
00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:49.570
We also owe the writers, and especially Greg Daniels,

35
00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:59.730
a big debt of gratitude in that they trust the actors enough to let us play with their lines and improvise off of them and come up with other line ideas and pitches.

36
00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:02.130
You don't get to do that on a lot of other TV shows.

37
00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:05.850
I think what helped it push through was a phenomenal cast and really great writing staff.

38
00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:08.950
The perfect man for the job in Greg Daniels.

39
00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:17.450
Greg Daniels said in our first meeting, he's like, you know, American comedy is like this big ship, you know, a big, like, cruise liner.

40
00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:23.150
And if you can just point it one degree in the right direction, you can make a big, big difference.

41
00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.510
You can't turn comedy that sharply.

42
00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:34.030
And I feel like that's what The Office did, is it took American comedy and it turned it one degree in the right direction.

43
00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:36.910
At the time, comedy was very silly.

44
00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.670
And there were a lot of very broad shows on the air.

45
00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:44.750
And I think it was just the perfect time for reality to hit comedy.

46
00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:50.010
I think that there was something sort of like it was lightning in a bottle for the entire cast and the entire creative team.

47
00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:55.070
It's kind of a troupe of people who understand writing and performing all at the same time.

48
00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:57.250
I spent more time here than I did on the set.

49
00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:59.310
I spent more time here than I did at home.

50
00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:04.530
I definitely spent more hours here over the past 10 years than anywhere else in the world.

51
00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:07.310
And it's not a very pretty place to be.

52
00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:11.390
But there was a lot of laughter and a lot of great ideas.

53
00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:15.850
Well, Greg really was the visionary behind this show.

54
00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:30.910
It was not an easy thing to adapt something that was only 13 episodes long, but a brilliant concept, and turn it into this 201 episodes of American television.

55
00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:33.330
I mean, that was Greg.

56
00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:34.010
Yeah.

57
00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:35.610
And also our writers.

58
00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:38.210
He assembled such an amazing team.

59
00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:45.750
And, you know, as Jen and I have done this rewatch, those of you that listen know how gracious the writing staff has been and Greg.

60
00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:47.070
They've come on this show.

61
00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:50.490
They have sent us in answers and audio clips.

62
00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:53.210
And we're just so appreciative to them.

63
00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:57.490
Well, Lady, you shared in our book that you had a writing professor who said,

64
00:03:57.490 --> 00:04:00.290
If something is a pleasure to do, it's a pleasure to watch.

65
00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.390
And I think that's what BJ was saying in that clip.

66
00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:09.290
Like, it was my pleasure to sit in this dumpy writer's room for 10 years.

67
00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:12.950
If you watch it on the DVD, he is in the writer's room.

68
00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.910
And there's not much there, you know.

69
00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:15.370
No, no.

70
00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.050
But it is true.

71
00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:22.630
We just all had such a joyful time doing this show.

72
00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.530
And I think people feel it when they watch it.

73
00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:26.070
Yeah.

74
00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:28.790
Well, Angela, I loved your lookbacks.

75
00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:29.590
Thanks.

76
00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:30.970
I enjoyed watching that.

77
00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:33.530
I couldn't watch it, everybody.

78
00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.070
I told Angela, I'm like, I'll be a puddle.

79
00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:37.430
I can't do it.

80
00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:39.350
I said, Jenna, do you want to watch it together?

81
00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:40.810
And you were just like, no.

82
00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.510
Well, I was a puddle.

83
00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:43.230
So, yeah.

84
00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:50.050
I'll say I haven't watched the finale until we had to watch it to break it down.

85
00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.390
Because I don't know if this is true.

86
00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:54.830
And I actually wish we would have asked Billie Eilish this.

87
00:04:54.830 --> 00:05:00.590
I know some people who will watch the whole series, but they won't watch the finale.

88
00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:02.610
Oh, man.

89
00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:04.910
They're missing some really good nuggets.

90
00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:05.750
I know.

91
00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:06.230
I know.

92
00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:08.870
And actually, I'm glad now that I've seen it.

93
00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:09.410
But yeah.

94
00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:12.730
Well, I'll tell you what I did after I watched The Look Back.

95
00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:16.450
And I recommend that you do this because it's really emotional.

96
00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:19.510
I then watched the season nine bloopers.

97
00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:20.830
Oh, no.

98
00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:22.730
And then I was just laughing.

99
00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:25.230
So, I went from tearing up to laughter.

100
00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:27.290
And that's the way you got to do it.

101
00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:28.290
All right.

102
00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.630
Well, let's move on to fast fact number two.

103
00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:33.430
I'm calling this one Wedding Weather.

104
00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:34.030
Yeah.

105
00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:38.430
We shot all of Angela and Dwight's wedding at Big Sky Ranch.

106
00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:41.370
We shot for three days at the ranch.

107
00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:44.150
We shot on a Thursday, a Friday, and a Sunday.

108
00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:46.410
Thursday was actually my birthday.

109
00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:47.490
Oh, yeah.

110
00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:48.150
That's right.

111
00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:50.070
It was also the day Steve was there.

112
00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:51.170
Oh.

113
00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:54.650
So, that was a really, really fun memory for me from that birthday.

114
00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:57.390
But there was an issue.

115
00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:00.930
Like any real wedding, we couldn't control the weather.

116
00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:03.130
And it was crazy windy.

117
00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:05.090
It was cold.

118
00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:06.390
It rained.

119
00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:08.870
The high was 61.

120
00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:10.270
The low was 45.

121
00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:11.210
Yeah.

122
00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:14.690
I remember them being worried the tent would blow away.

123
00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:16.250
They were waiting it down.

124
00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:17.970
The lanterns were swaying.

125
00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:21.270
You saw the cloud bank rolling in.

126
00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:25.950
Well, I remember wondering, are we able to shoot this?

127
00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:26.330
Yeah.

128
00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:31.250
Because the sky was very, very gloomy and ominous.

129
00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:39.230
And Matt Soane actually had to put up all these giant lights and like floodlights in order to try to brighten up everything.

130
00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:40.070
It was dark.

131
00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:40.950
It was.

132
00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:41.450
Yeah.

133
00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:47.330
But the call sheets for these three days, they said, we will shoot rain or shine.

134
00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:48.450
Please be prepared.

135
00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:49.370
Yep.

136
00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:54.830
And we have some great, great pictures that really showcase the windy conditions.

137
00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:58.010
I mean, I have one of the clouds rolling in.

138
00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:03.650
I don't know if you remember, Jenna, but my veil kept blowing all over my face.

139
00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:03.990
I do.

140
00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:07.910
I have a picture of me and John and the veil is about to wrap around us.

141
00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:14.190
But our favorite, hands down, is a photo we discovered when we wrote our book, The Office BFFs.

142
00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:21.490
I took the picture standing in Angela Martin's shallow grave of everyone looking back at me.

143
00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:25.610
I really wanted to remember what I saw on Angela's wedding day.

144
00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:28.590
And I took that picture and I never thought anything about it.

145
00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:29.370
You know, we looked at it.

146
00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:30.390
I put it in a scrapbook.

147
00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:37.050
But when we started to do our book, we were really zooming in on pictures to make sure the image was good, the quality was good.

148
00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:40.950
And Catherine is so funny.

149
00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:43.930
I can't believe we didn't see it for years.

150
00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:44.450
I know.

151
00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:46.470
Catherine in this picture.

152
00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:47.910
Everyone looks cold.

153
00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:48.970
Jenna, you look freezing.

154
00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:52.090
Kate Flannery is actually doing a thing with her face like, ooh.

155
00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:58.470
Like, but Catherine's face is completely covered by her hair.

156
00:07:58.650 --> 00:07:58.790
Yeah.

157
00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:00.250
It's hilarious.

158
00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:03.090
We'll put it in stories.

159
00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:10.370
I also found in my digital clutter an email from our key second assistant director, Stephanie.

160
00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:11.810
Oh, my gosh.

161
00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:14.030
I was just texting with Stephanie recently.

162
00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:15.750
I love her.

163
00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:21.450
Remember I told you I went to that birthday party where we discussed whether or not the birthday boy.

164
00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:21.950
Oh, yes.

165
00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:22.990
Was, right?

166
00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:23.370
Right.

167
00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:23.630
Okay.

168
00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:24.450
Shower grower.

169
00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:24.970
Right.

170
00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:34.850
So I thought, oh, the morning after the birthday party, I'm going to send a fun text to all the ladies about, you know, some inside joke from the party.

171
00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:40.630
So I send it to my friends, Michelle, Anne, and Steph.

172
00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:42.170
Oh, no.

173
00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:43.770
You texted the wrong Stephanie.

174
00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:44.810
Texted the wrong Stephanie.

175
00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:56.770
And so Steph, our second AD, after a while of us not hearing from Steph, who was at the party, she texts back, hey, ladies, this sounds like a really fun party.

176
00:08:56.990 --> 00:08:57.070
Oh, no.

177
00:08:57.070 --> 00:09:01.130
But I think you mean this for a different Steph.

178
00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:02.230
Oh, no.

179
00:09:03.030 --> 00:09:07.050
But anyway, and then I was, like, texting her on the side and was like, how are you, though?

180
00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:08.730
All right.

181
00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:09.510
So go ahead.

182
00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:10.730
Steph sent an email.

183
00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:11.470
She did.

184
00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:13.930
It was to the entire cast, and here's what it said.

185
00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:17.590
Hey, guys, I'm looking forward to the giant days we have coming up.

186
00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:18.870
They should be a lot of fun.

187
00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:25.170
I am trying to make the days run as smoothly as possible and want to alert you to our plans in advance.

188
00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:32.050
Due to the nature of the set and the gorgeous views at the location, there is very little indoor space available to us.

189
00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:37.930
We are planning to take advantage of the remoteness of the set, and we will see 360.

190
00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:39.930
Oh, I remember this.

191
00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:40.410
Yeah.

192
00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:44.690
So that meant we do not have any holding areas planned.

193
00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:45.370
Yes.

194
00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:47.630
There were no trailers up there.

195
00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:49.830
The trailers were down this long hill.

196
00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:50.930
You had to take a van.

197
00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:59.390
So once we got ready at the bottom of the hill, you would take a van up to the top, and then you were just at this wedding.

198
00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:00.050
Right.

199
00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:06.770
Stephanie said, while we're shooting, there will be a small group of you who are working inside the house.

200
00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:08.250
This is a hot set.

201
00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:09.930
Please don't move anything around.

202
00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:10.770
Yep.

203
00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:14.150
So we were inside that house, Dwight's farmhouse.

204
00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:20.710
The other thing I wanted to note is she wrote, there are 33 principal actors working today.

205
00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:22.850
And 50 background performers.

206
00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:23.350
Yep.

207
00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:25.810
She wrote, we are preparing for rain.

208
00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:30.250
And lastly, please be aware that there is no cell phone service.

209
00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:33.570
My cell phone has not been working at this location.

210
00:10:33.890 --> 00:10:36.810
Production is renting a temporary cell phone.

211
00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.110
Please try me by that or email me.

212
00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:41.390
We were really in the middle of nowhere.

213
00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:45.110
She included directions, which were very detailed.

214
00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:47.850
And I remember that drive, don't you, Jenna?

215
00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:48.070
Yeah.

216
00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:51.410
In the morning, it was full fog and miSt.

217
00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:51.850
Yep.

218
00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:52.870
And we were driving.

219
00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:56.050
You would have thought we were sort of like in the highlands of Scotland.

220
00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:57.210
Yes, very much.

221
00:10:57.350 --> 00:10:58.350
That's a great comparison.

222
00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:00.950
We had to go through two different canyons.

223
00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:09.250
Well, I think that these conditions actually lent themselves to a really, really fun final shoot experience.

224
00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:15.690
It really reminded me of our early days on set when none of us had phones or working computers.

225
00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:16.050
Yeah.

226
00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:18.790
And we just would sit on set.

227
00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:19.870
And hang out.

228
00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.130
And that's what we did when we shot this wedding.

229
00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:23.530
We just hung out.

230
00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:24.750
And it was really fun.

231
00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:28.450
We hung out in parkas that had a piece of tape with our name on it.

232
00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:28.910
Mm-hmm.

233
00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:31.490
That's how we knew which parka was ours.

234
00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:32.750
It was super cold.

235
00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:33.410
So cold.

236
00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:36.670
And we just huddled up in that drafty house and talked and laughed.

237
00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:38.070
And it was great.

238
00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:39.870
All right.

239
00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:42.170
This is a big top of show, everybody.

240
00:11:42.170 --> 00:11:44.190
And I've got a big fast fact three.

241
00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:44.870
Yeah.

242
00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:50.690
Because we had a big guest star on this episode, Mr. Steve Carell.

243
00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:54.290
I still can't believe how they pulled this off.

244
00:11:54.410 --> 00:11:55.470
I really can't.

245
00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:57.690
We got a lot of fan mail about it.

246
00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:00.530
And I have a whole breakdown on how we made it work.

247
00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:02.890
Let's get into these fan questions.

248
00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:04.430
Bailey E.

249
00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:06.330
from Manitoba said,

250
00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:12.130
One of the scenes from The Office that never fails to make me cry is when Michael comes back to be Dwight's best man.

251
00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:16.730
I've always wondered whose idea was it to have Steve Carell come back.

252
00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:18.910
And was it a surprise to the cast?

253
00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:21.670
And Megan Kaye from Tampa, Florida said,

254
00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:25.270
I'd love to know your lady's feelings on Steve coming back to the set.

255
00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:28.030
But in the opening credits, his name is not mentioned.

256
00:12:28.030 --> 00:12:31.130
So it was a huge surprise for viewers to see.

257
00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:34.790
I absolutely bawl every time I see it.

258
00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:37.250
And I would love to know how it all came together.

259
00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:38.930
And Hugo S.

260
00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:40.330
from Kyoto, Japan said,

261
00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:44.190
What was the process in getting Steve to return for his final episode?

262
00:12:44.710 --> 00:12:48.810
Well, Jenna, you know everything that was happening behind the scenes that the rest of us didn't know.

263
00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:49.750
So you have to share.

264
00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:51.030
All right.

265
00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:53.990
Well, it was Greg's idea to have Steve come back.

266
00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:56.250
He had wanted that for a very long time.

267
00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.570
And he asked him pretty early in season nine.

268
00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:00.910
But Steve was reluctant.

269
00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:05.210
He felt like Michael's story had really ended.

270
00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:08.310
He didn't want to open it back up again.

271
00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:16.490
And he especially did not want to come back after two years and have this finale episode be about him.

272
00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:19.910
Steve really felt like my character had his ending.

273
00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:21.770
This is everybody else's ending.

274
00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:23.770
And he didn't want to overshadow that.

275
00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:25.610
Well, he's very gracious that way.

276
00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:26.130
Yeah.

277
00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:32.770
But then Greg had the idea of the final episode being Dwight and Angela's wedding.

278
00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:36.230
And Steve agreed Michael would be there.

279
00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:37.710
I believe that.

280
00:13:37.890 --> 00:13:40.710
I believe Michael would want to be there for Dwight and Angela.

281
00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:41.370
Yeah.

282
00:13:41.530 --> 00:13:46.530
It was a creative reason that was supported by history, you know?

283
00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:52.890
So I remember being up in the writer's room with John when we found out that Steve was going to come back.

284
00:13:53.510 --> 00:13:55.730
And we were sworn to secrecy.

285
00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:59.230
And this was, like, really epic to pull off.

286
00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:00.470
I've told this story before.

287
00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:05.370
Rainn Wilson turned to me and he said, not even Angela, Jenna.

288
00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:07.190
I was like, okay.

289
00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:07.870
So aggressive.

290
00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:09.930
I mean, he knows I tell you everything.

291
00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:10.490
I know.

292
00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:12.770
It was really hard not to tell you.

293
00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:19.090
Because, Ang, you did not find out until he showed up on set that day.

294
00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:20.850
Oh, I know the exact moment.

295
00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:23.830
I had driven through the two canyons.

296
00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:25.310
I had taken the dirt road.

297
00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.450
I was at our base camp in the middle of nowhere.

298
00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.630
Where it was cold and foggy.

299
00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:38.370
And right as I was getting to hair and makeup, the set PA turned to me and said, oh, Steve is here.

300
00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:40.510
And I said, what are you talking about?

301
00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:44.650
And at first I thought she meant Steve Burgess.

302
00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:47.790
And she was like, Steve Carell is here.

303
00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:49.010
I said, what?

304
00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:51.250
And I opened the door.

305
00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:52.990
And there he was.

306
00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:54.790
He was sitting in hair and makeup.

307
00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:58.370
And I just was like, Steve.

308
00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:02.600
And I just hugged him.

309
00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:03.680
And we were laughing.

310
00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:04.820
I couldn't believe it.

311
00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.060
I was like so confused.

312
00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:09.200
And then we just got to chat in hair and makeup.

313
00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:10.960
And it was absolutely wonderful.

314
00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:13.780
I remember the vibe in the hair and makeup trailer.

315
00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:15.340
When he was in there.

316
00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:16.220
Buzzing.

317
00:15:16.420 --> 00:15:16.560
Yeah.

318
00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:17.500
A body buzz.

319
00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:20.380
Everybody was like, it was a party.

320
00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:20.800
Yeah.

321
00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:27.640
Well, this was really crazy because Greg did not tell NBC that Steve was coming back.

322
00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:33.200
Well, this is what I remember at the table read when all the NBC suits were there, all the executives.

323
00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:36.140
In the script, it was Creed.

324
00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:37.660
Right?

325
00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:38.260
Yeah.

326
00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:39.780
So that's the thing.

327
00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:46.880
When you turn in a script, they use those script pages, those locations, those scenes to set a budget for your episode.

328
00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:53.500
And so they had a scene at our table read between Dwight and Jim.

329
00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:56.380
But it wasn't the scene that ended up in the show.

330
00:15:56.460 --> 00:15:57.480
But there was a scene.

331
00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:03.420
It was a placeholder of Jim helping Dwight right before it's time to go to the wedding.

332
00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:08.680
Same number of lines, same page count as the real scene with Steve.

333
00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:17.380
And then later, Michael has a talking head where he says, oh, it's like all my kids grew up and they got married.

334
00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:18.940
Creed read that.

335
00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:19.600
Yes.

336
00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:21.340
At the table read, Creed read it.

337
00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:22.720
It was a Creed talking head.

338
00:16:22.820 --> 00:16:23.700
It got a laugh.

339
00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:24.200
It did.

340
00:16:25.180 --> 00:16:27.040
So no one at NBC knew.

341
00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:27.580
No.

342
00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:35.760
And Steve Burgess told me that NBC has a rule that nobody can be filmed for the show without a signed contract.

343
00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:44.360
So in order to follow the rules and still keep the secret, Steve Carell signed a contract to do the show for this episode.

344
00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:50.600
But Steve Burgess kept it locked in his desk drawer until the day the show aired.

345
00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:51.760
Steve Burgess?

346
00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:53.300
So he could be like, no, no, no.

347
00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:54.200
Look at the date.

348
00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.260
I had a contract.

349
00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:58.500
I just forgot to hand it in.

350
00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:01.340
This is some serious maneuvering.

351
00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:02.440
There's more, lady.

352
00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:08.440
So usually every day after you shoot, you send those tapes into the studio.

353
00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:09.600
They're called the dailies.

354
00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:09.940
Right.

355
00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:13.780
For them to review if they have something they didn't like, they want to take out.

356
00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:14.200
Yep.

357
00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:14.760
Yada, yada.

358
00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:16.840
They didn't send Steve scenes.

359
00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:19.800
They kept them locked up somewhere else.

360
00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:28.660
And then Dave Rogers did a cut of the episode because the network has to give notes, sent a Steve-less version.

361
00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:34.160
So there's a lot of people in cahoots here to keep Steve's appearance a secret.

362
00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:36.500
And I know Greg had a specific reason.

363
00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:37.320
Share it, Jenna.

364
00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:47.460
He was afraid that if he turned in any footage of Steve Carell on the show before it aired, that NBC would make promos out of it and ruin the surprise.

365
00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:49.540
Oh, they would want the ratings for sure.

366
00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:49.820
Right?

367
00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:50.280
Yeah.

368
00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:52.600
And then it wouldn't have been a surprise.

369
00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:53.500
I get that.

370
00:17:53.500 --> 00:18:00.480
So finally, we had our final cut, the version that we had to turn in to the network with Steve.

371
00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:01.340
With Steve.

372
00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:03.160
But we weren't turning it in.

373
00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:09.860
And I guess NBC finally put their foot down and said, we will not air something that no one here has seen.

374
00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:20.280
So Greg and Steve Burgess and Dave Rogers and Claire Scanlon said, you can come stand in our edit bay and watch it.

375
00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:23.900
But did that piss him off?

376
00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:26.640
I'm sure none of this never happens.

377
00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:30.000
Steve Burgess was like, I'll never work in this town again.

378
00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:31.700
And Greg was like, it'll be fine.

379
00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:41.780
So Steve Burgess said, you should have seen their faces as they're standing in the edit bay the day before the episode was going to air.

380
00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:45.940
Were they so grumpy that they had to come to our studios and stand in that edit bay?

381
00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:53.140
He said, when they saw Steve come on, there was this mixture of them being like so pissed and so excited.

382
00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:59.460
And Dave Rogers said that they waited until 9 a.m.

383
00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:03.260
the day the finale aired to actually hand over the episode.

384
00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:04.040
Wow.

385
00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:07.080
Is that the greatest kept secret?

386
00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:09.280
I mean, yeah.

387
00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:12.740
It's got to be one of the best kept secrets in television.

388
00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:14.880
I would have been so stressed.

389
00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:15.740
I would have been horrible.

390
00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:16.540
But also.

391
00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:17.540
I'm so glad I didn't know.

392
00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:18.320
I'm so glad.

393
00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:21.720
I was so excited when you finally knew.

394
00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:22.220
I was like, ah.

395
00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:25.860
But I mean, even that, like we still had to keep the secret till it aired.

396
00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:26.240
Oh, yeah.

397
00:19:26.400 --> 00:19:30.560
We did so much press and everybody asked us if Steve was coming back.

398
00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:35.220
David Letterman asked John Krasinski if Steve was coming back and John lied to him.

399
00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:35.500
Yeah.

400
00:19:35.720 --> 00:19:36.480
Lied to his face.

401
00:19:36.660 --> 00:19:37.740
Lied to David Letterman.

402
00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:38.160
David Letterman.

403
00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:41.940
And no, we were asked tons of questions about the finale.

404
00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:48.100
And Greg sent out an email and was like, I need you all to come together and not say a word on this.

405
00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:49.440
And we didn't.

406
00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:50.000
Mm-hmm.

407
00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:51.140
All right.

