00:29:56.700 --> 00:29:58.640
This is the song the writers wanted.

639
00:29:58.980 --> 00:30:03.840
But since we did not use Guns N' Roses singing it, it was allowed.

640
00:30:03.840 --> 00:30:06.400
But it still cost $50,000.

641
00:30:07.020 --> 00:30:07.580
Damn.

642
00:30:08.140 --> 00:30:10.020
Just to have a string quartet play it.

643
00:30:10.340 --> 00:30:11.260
Popular song.

644
00:30:11.440 --> 00:30:11.880
Wow.

645
00:30:12.200 --> 00:30:18.540
I have to think that Angela and Dwight had a few arguments over the song choices for the wedding.

646
00:30:18.740 --> 00:30:19.300
You think so?

647
00:30:19.400 --> 00:30:24.900
I don't think Angela would have picked Sweet Child of Mine as her entrance.

648
00:30:24.900 --> 00:30:27.560
We got a fan question from Jenna F.

649
00:30:27.580 --> 00:30:29.400
in Los Angeles who said,

650
00:30:29.540 --> 00:30:37.740
This seemingly simple bit of Phyllis carrying you down the aisle actually required a pretty elaborate set of circumstances to pull off.

651
00:30:37.900 --> 00:30:40.540
You wrote about it in your book, The Office BFFs.

652
00:30:40.620 --> 00:30:42.840
But Angela, will you tell the story on the podcast?

653
00:30:43.280 --> 00:30:45.160
Thank you, Jenna F., for writing in.

654
00:30:45.300 --> 00:30:48.920
You've been a loyal writer, commentator on this podcaSt.

655
00:30:49.660 --> 00:30:52.820
Well, this is how it was described in the shooting draft.

656
00:30:53.440 --> 00:31:00.420
Dwight stands in a shallow grave with an empty one next to him, beside Jim and Andy and the ushers under a bower of flowers.

657
00:31:00.700 --> 00:31:06.660
The guests are in suits and look great, seated on hay bales with white cloths covering the tops.

658
00:31:06.660 --> 00:31:12.440
Phyllis walks down the aisle with Angela riding on her back, smiling and nodding to all the guests.

659
00:31:12.740 --> 00:31:17.740
When she gets to the front, Angela daintily steps off and into the grave next to Dwight.

660
00:31:18.320 --> 00:31:24.880
But to make this walk down the aisle happen, well, first of all, Phyllis could not carry me down the aisle.

661
00:31:25.080 --> 00:31:26.620
That was not safe for her to do.

662
00:31:27.200 --> 00:31:35.140
So they actually got a stunt woman that had Phyllis' similar hair color that carried me down the aisle.

663
00:31:35.520 --> 00:31:37.100
And we had to practice this.

664
00:31:37.220 --> 00:31:37.980
I had a rehearsal.

665
00:31:38.400 --> 00:31:41.660
So we had to set up two different angles for the camera.

666
00:31:42.100 --> 00:31:49.800
The camera that would be behind Phyllis and I walking down the aisle were really filming me on the back of the stunt woman.

667
00:31:49.940 --> 00:31:50.280
Okay.

668
00:31:50.280 --> 00:31:51.500
Because you couldn't see her face.

669
00:31:51.640 --> 00:31:52.980
And I am really being carried.

670
00:31:52.980 --> 00:31:55.100
And that's why you see my legs dangling.

671
00:31:55.520 --> 00:31:55.840
Right?

672
00:31:56.060 --> 00:31:56.320
Yes.

673
00:31:56.620 --> 00:32:00.620
But, of course, they also needed a shot of us coming towards the camera.

674
00:32:01.020 --> 00:32:13.020
And as we walked towards the camera, it was actually Phyllis and me behind her on this wooden plank being held by two men.

675
00:32:13.700 --> 00:32:14.200
Yes.

676
00:32:14.420 --> 00:32:18.720
And we had to practice the walk together because Phyllis does one step together.

677
00:32:18.940 --> 00:32:23.880
You know that traditional kind of walk down the aisle where you take one step and then your feet come together and you take one step.

678
00:32:24.040 --> 00:32:25.400
So we had to practice this.

679
00:32:25.400 --> 00:32:34.500
And there was one time where Phyllis got too far ahead and my arms are on her neck and the men with the plank did not meet her and I almost fell off the thing.

680
00:32:34.500 --> 00:32:36.440
It was such a crazy thing.

681
00:32:36.440 --> 00:32:40.220
It was such a crazy thing to see, Angela, because we're all sitting there being the wedding guests.

682
00:32:40.220 --> 00:32:48.280
And, you know, the two guys holding you on a piece of wood and you're sort of holding on to Phyllis.

683
00:32:48.420 --> 00:32:51.940
And then they removed the guys in poSt.

684
00:32:52.160 --> 00:32:52.880
And the wood.

685
00:32:53.560 --> 00:32:59.100
Which is so crazy to me because I remember I turned to John and I was like, I don't understand.

686
00:32:59.740 --> 00:33:01.340
We can just paint them out.

687
00:33:01.520 --> 00:33:03.340
We can just get rid of them.

688
00:33:03.620 --> 00:33:03.820
Yeah.

689
00:33:03.820 --> 00:33:04.860
He was like, uh-huh.

690
00:33:05.060 --> 00:33:05.460
They did.

691
00:33:05.940 --> 00:33:08.040
There's a whole wooden plank in two men.

692
00:33:08.400 --> 00:33:14.440
You wouldn't expect that on The Office there would be like an elaborate special effects moment.

693
00:33:14.900 --> 00:33:15.240
Mm-hmm.

694
00:33:15.520 --> 00:33:16.380
But this was.

695
00:33:16.540 --> 00:33:21.160
This was of the caliber of something you might see in The Matrix, dare I say.

696
00:33:21.460 --> 00:33:21.980
Exactly.

697
00:33:22.320 --> 00:33:24.380
Oh, thank you for bringing The Matrix into the finale.

698
00:33:24.380 --> 00:33:28.280
I needed Keanu to be here with us in some way for the finale.

699
00:33:28.420 --> 00:33:29.480
I really appreciate that.

700
00:33:29.480 --> 00:33:34.780
There are so many things that have happened to us over the last five years since we have been making this podcaSt.

701
00:33:34.780 --> 00:33:36.480
I was going over them in my head.

702
00:33:36.600 --> 00:33:42.920
I was thinking of life and just world events and all kinds of things.

703
00:33:43.620 --> 00:33:52.000
And I was filled with such gratitude for all the things that we've done, you know, over these five years.

704
00:33:52.800 --> 00:33:55.580
But I thought, I am not done here, though.

705
00:33:56.160 --> 00:33:57.480
I am not done.

706
00:33:57.480 --> 00:34:05.120
And the one thing, the one thing that we have not managed to capture in this five years is Keanu.

707
00:34:05.820 --> 00:34:06.660
I know.

708
00:34:06.860 --> 00:34:09.640
And so we cannot stop podcasting.

709
00:34:10.020 --> 00:34:10.580
Until.

710
00:34:10.920 --> 00:34:12.400
Until we have that.

711
00:34:12.620 --> 00:34:14.460
Until we get to interview Keanu.

712
00:34:14.880 --> 00:34:18.780
You know, he's going to be on Broadway and waiting for Godot with Alex Winter.

713
00:34:20.400 --> 00:34:22.120
And that's next fall.

714
00:34:22.180 --> 00:34:25.160
And I feel like that's a reason to come talk to us.

715
00:34:26.240 --> 00:34:27.820
Maybe we go to the play.

716
00:34:28.380 --> 00:34:30.560
And then we talk to him in New York City.

717
00:34:31.060 --> 00:34:35.680
Well, lady, you know, any reason to go to New York City and see a play, I'm all over it.

718
00:34:36.360 --> 00:34:36.840
Done.

719
00:34:37.120 --> 00:34:37.520
Done.

720
00:34:37.520 --> 00:34:43.080
I do want to say, while we've been talking, our balloons that say congrats have fallen.

721
00:34:46.300 --> 00:34:48.640
They're hanging on by one string.

722
00:34:48.920 --> 00:34:51.300
We have a few other things to cover from this scene.

723
00:34:51.880 --> 00:34:58.300
Number one, I want to say I think Greg Daniels should have won an Emmy for this episode, in particular for all these wedding scenes.

724
00:34:58.580 --> 00:35:00.300
They are so funny.

725
00:35:00.400 --> 00:35:00.960
So funny.

726
00:35:01.060 --> 00:35:01.920
And so well done.

727
00:35:01.920 --> 00:35:10.820
Again, I love that even though Angela Martin is on Phyllis's back, she is still waving to people who are seated.

728
00:35:11.040 --> 00:35:13.840
Kind of awkwardly, my hand is in Phyllis's face.

729
00:35:13.840 --> 00:35:17.620
I'm holding a bouquet in the other hand while I'm trying to hold on.

730
00:35:18.300 --> 00:35:22.500
I love that Kevin fist bumps Angela and she fist bumps him back.

731
00:35:22.660 --> 00:35:25.480
And Meredith gives her real enthusiastic thumbs up.

732
00:35:25.720 --> 00:35:27.160
Those were improv moments.

733
00:35:27.500 --> 00:35:29.840
And it's just such a happy thing.

734
00:35:29.840 --> 00:35:33.800
And then when Angela crawls into her, Michael comes over and gives her a hug.

735
00:35:33.920 --> 00:35:34.980
That was not in the script.

736
00:35:35.300 --> 00:35:36.760
Steve did that in the moment.

737
00:35:37.340 --> 00:35:38.880
And I love it.

738
00:35:39.040 --> 00:35:40.700
I'm just so happy to see him.

739
00:35:40.800 --> 00:35:42.040
I'm hugging him for real.

740
00:35:42.840 --> 00:35:44.300
31 minutes, 6 seconds.

741
00:35:44.440 --> 00:35:47.700
I want to give a shout out to the couple who I assume are playing Angela's parents.

742
00:35:47.820 --> 00:35:51.040
They're in the front row, both tiny folks, both blonde.

743
00:35:51.040 --> 00:36:00.140
And then when Oscar comes down the aisle with Philip, the woman playing Angela's mother is just gazing at Philip like a grandma would.

744
00:36:00.820 --> 00:36:04.100
I also want to give a shout out to Michael Tuba Hethernton.

745
00:36:04.220 --> 00:36:05.180
He is back.

746
00:36:05.180 --> 00:36:06.300
He is the minister.

747
00:36:07.160 --> 00:36:09.080
And he's going to marry Dwight and Angela.

748
00:36:09.560 --> 00:36:12.540
Yes, that's Veda's husband, Veda, our script supervisor.

749
00:36:12.540 --> 00:36:14.600
