Yes.

2018
01:31:05.940 --> 01:31:13.980
If you go to 48 minutes and 14 seconds, that shot of all of us leaving was actually the last shot we filmed together as a caSt.

2019
01:31:14.260 --> 01:31:14.720
Yeah.

2020
01:31:14.980 --> 01:31:17.520
So, Pam has the final talking head.

2021
01:31:17.660 --> 01:31:25.080
And when the one-liner, which is the schedule of scenes for an episode, comes out, you know I would love to read it.

2022
01:31:25.200 --> 01:31:25.580
Mm-hmm.

2023
01:31:25.580 --> 01:31:33.300
I saw that the very last thing that was scheduled for the last day of shooting was Pam's talking head.

2024
01:31:33.760 --> 01:31:38.140
I went to John's trailer, and I said, John, did you see the one-liner?

2025
01:31:39.160 --> 01:31:42.480
And I showed him, and I said, I don't want to be here alone.

2026
01:31:43.000 --> 01:31:45.180
I don't want to be here all by myself.

2027
01:31:45.820 --> 01:31:46.280
Yeah.

2028
01:31:46.280 --> 01:31:48.100
I want us to end together.

2029
01:31:48.380 --> 01:31:50.440
And John said, we have to end together.

2030
01:31:51.080 --> 01:32:06.520
So we went together to Ken Kwapis and Greg, and they said, oh, we thought it would be really poetic to end the show by filming the very last moment last, but we hear you.

2031
01:32:06.520 --> 01:32:08.260
So here's what we'll do.

2032
01:32:08.640 --> 01:32:12.360
We're going to film your talking head, if everyone doesn't mind waiting.

2033
01:32:13.020 --> 01:32:21.620
And then when you're finished, we will film that final B-roll of everyone leaving the office and of Pam taking the watercolor off the wall.

2034
01:32:21.780 --> 01:32:22.720
How does that sound?

2035
01:32:23.000 --> 01:32:29.980
And John and I were like, yes, we need to all be together when you say that's a wrap on The Office.

2036
01:32:30.500 --> 01:32:32.180
That's a series wrap.

2037
01:32:32.360 --> 01:32:33.940
I'm like, I don't want to be here by myself.

2038
01:32:34.100 --> 01:32:34.280
Yeah.

2039
01:32:34.620 --> 01:32:34.780
Yeah.

2040
01:32:35.440 --> 01:32:36.860
And that's what they did.

2041
01:32:36.860 --> 01:32:38.780
And we were all so thankful.

2042
01:32:39.460 --> 01:32:43.700
And, you know, I have video of all of us watching you do that talking head.

2043
01:32:43.960 --> 01:32:45.860
I'm finally going to post it.

2044
01:32:46.020 --> 01:32:47.740
I've been saving it for years.

2045
01:32:49.120 --> 01:32:57.120
And it was just really moving that when they said that's a wrap, that we all just poured into the bullpen.

2046
01:32:57.360 --> 01:33:03.040
Our crew, our writers were all standing around waiting, watching with us on the stage.

2047
01:33:03.040 --> 01:33:06.380
And we all just hugged and cried, all of us.

2048
01:33:06.800 --> 01:33:10.240
Well, we did that exit way more times than we needed to.

2049
01:33:10.480 --> 01:33:10.980
I know.

2050
01:33:10.980 --> 01:33:18.240
And Ken Kwapis said, after about like six times, he turned to Greg and he said, Greg, I think we got it.

2051
01:33:18.520 --> 01:33:18.940
We're done.

2052
01:33:19.220 --> 01:33:21.180
And Greg said, what do we do?

2053
01:33:21.840 --> 01:33:28.420
And Ken said, well, we have to say that's a wrap, but I think you should say it, Greg.

2054
01:33:29.380 --> 01:33:32.140
So he said, I'll have him do it one more time, okay?

2055
01:33:32.440 --> 01:33:33.700
And Greg was like, okay.

2056
01:33:34.120 --> 01:33:35.860
So we did it one more time.

2057
01:33:36.160 --> 01:33:40.400
And I remember every time we would leave, we would crowd.

2058
01:33:40.480 --> 01:33:43.940
All of us would crowd into that little area by the elevator.

2059
01:33:44.400 --> 01:33:46.680
And we would stand there for a beat.

2060
01:33:47.040 --> 01:33:52.060
And then you would hear them say, all right, reset, back to one, going again.

2061
01:33:53.560 --> 01:33:56.420
And there was always this very pregnant pause.

2062
01:33:56.560 --> 01:34:01.760
Like once we got to like take three, take four, you're like, how many times can we do this?

2063
01:34:02.240 --> 01:34:06.100
And then finally, we were all standing there in that like pregnant pause.

2064
01:34:06.240 --> 01:34:07.720
And we heard Greg's voice.

2065
01:34:07.900 --> 01:34:08.020
Yeah.

2066
01:34:08.020 --> 01:34:13.520
He said, cut, that's a wrap, that's a series wrap on the office.

2067
01:34:13.780 --> 01:34:18.000
And then we all came out from that area.

2068
01:34:18.300 --> 01:34:21.780
And we were surprised by our crew that they had had gather.

2069
01:34:22.680 --> 01:34:22.840
Yeah.

2070
01:34:23.620 --> 01:34:27.180
Every time we walked to the elevator bank, I was next to Phyllis.

2071
01:34:27.300 --> 01:34:32.340
Because when you watch the scene, Dwight goes to help with the plant.

2072
01:34:32.340 --> 01:34:35.220
And I'm kind of left perched on top of front reception.

2073
01:34:35.220 --> 01:34:36.140
It's pretty high.

2074
01:34:37.100 --> 01:34:39.700
And Phyllis and Oscar would help me down.

2075
01:34:40.340 --> 01:34:42.100
So I would walk out with them.

2076
01:34:42.260 --> 01:34:46.180
And Phyllis and I would hold hands waiting to see if we would go again.

2077
01:34:47.860 --> 01:34:48.460
Yeah.

2078
01:34:49.180 --> 01:34:52.140
That was pretty emotional.

2079
01:34:53.740 --> 01:34:58.220
But the episode ends after Pam's talking head.

2080
01:34:59.140 --> 01:34:59.740
Yes.

2081
01:34:59.900 --> 01:35:03.260
Pam famously says there's a lot of beauty in ordinary things.

2082
01:35:03.380 --> 01:35:04.560
Isn't that kind of the point?

2083
01:35:04.560 --> 01:35:10.300
Well, that's just, that was Greg's philosophy of this show.

2084
01:35:10.540 --> 01:35:17.520
It was meant to mine the beauty in ordinary day-to-day life.

2085
01:35:17.820 --> 01:35:18.780
It's beautiful.

2086
01:35:19.120 --> 01:35:19.280
Yeah.

2087
01:35:19.440 --> 01:35:21.420
That's what we were shining a spotlight on.

2088
01:35:22.280 --> 01:35:23.640
So amazing.

2089
01:35:27.260 --> 01:35:29.660
And I loved shooting this talking head.

2090
01:35:29.840 --> 01:35:31.340
I was talking to Ken Quapis.

2091
01:35:31.480 --> 01:35:35.800
That's who was sitting across from me in the job when Jim finally asked Pam on a date.

2092
01:35:36.260 --> 01:35:39.480
And that's who I got to deliver my final talking head to.

2093
01:35:40.240 --> 01:35:42.180
And it's very meaningful to me.

2094
01:35:44.000 --> 01:35:47.280
I love that we see Steve again one last time.

2095
01:35:47.560 --> 01:35:49.760
I love that we get to see Michael.

2096
01:35:50.020 --> 01:35:51.960
And he's hanging Hope in a frame.

2097
01:35:52.320 --> 01:35:52.780
Mm-hmm.

2098
01:35:53.100 --> 01:35:54.000
That's right.

2099
01:35:54.460 --> 01:36:01.100
And then that sort of morphs into our actual building.

2100
01:36:01.100 --> 01:36:04.620
They sort of go from the watercolor to the actual Dunder Mifflin.

2101
01:36:04.780 --> 01:36:05.220
Mm-hmm.

2102
01:36:05.220 --> 01:36:07.520
And I love how plain it is.

2103
01:36:07.960 --> 01:36:13.840
I love, it's literally the most ordinary-looking building you could imagine.

2104
01:36:13.980 --> 01:36:14.160
Yeah.

2105
01:36:14.320 --> 01:36:15.540
And that was our building.

2106
01:36:15.860 --> 01:36:16.140
Yeah.

2107
01:36:16.580 --> 01:36:19.140
And Pam gets to take her painting home.

2108
01:36:19.320 --> 01:36:20.920
And Jenna took it home, too.

2109
01:36:21.440 --> 01:36:22.900
It's in my living room.

2110
01:36:24.020 --> 01:36:31.860
Well, guys, that is finale part two, but we're not finished yet because from the moment we

2111
01:36:31.860 --> 01:36:36.200
started this podcast, we knew exactly how we wanted to end it.

2112
01:36:36.400 --> 01:36:37.260
We did.

2113
01:36:37.580 --> 01:36:45.020
And my neighbor is coming through for us because we reached out to Creed Bratton and we said,

2114
01:36:45.160 --> 01:36:48.400
Creed, will you sing your song on our podcast, All the Faces?

2115
01:36:48.780 --> 01:36:52.320
That's the perfect way to say goodbye to this rewatch.

2116
01:36:52.320 --> 01:36:54.920
And he said yes, and he's here today.

2117
01:36:55.620 --> 01:37:01.100
So give us a second, which to you will literally feel like one second, and he's going to set

2118
01:37:01.100 --> 01:37:03.240
up and we'll chat with him.

2119
01:37:07.480 --> 01:37:10.600
Well, here is our special guest we've been talking about.

2120
01:37:10.600 --> 01:37:11.660
We are so excited.

2121
01:37:11.840 --> 01:37:18.060
In fact, our very first guest in our new space here to celebrate the end of the rewatch with

2122
01:37:18.060 --> 01:37:19.620
us is Creed Bratton.

2123
01:37:19.820 --> 01:37:20.480
Hi, Creed.

2124
01:37:20.780 --> 01:37:21.380
Hi, ladies.

2125
01:37:21.740 --> 01:37:22.800
Thanks for having me.

2126
01:37:23.140 --> 01:37:23.880
Yes, thank you.

2127
01:37:24.220 --> 01:37:25.160
You are here.

2128
01:37:25.160 --> 01:37:28.280
You are going to be leaving tomorrow.

2129
01:37:28.320 --> 01:37:31.620
We got you on your last day in town.

2130
01:37:31.920 --> 01:37:33.040
Tell everybody where you're going.

2131
01:37:33.320 --> 01:37:42.190
I'll be in Ireland and England, Norway, Denmark, Holland, Slovakia, and Czechoslovakia.

2132
01:37:42.940 --> 01:37:43.680
On tour.

2133
01:37:43.960 --> 01:37:45.240
On tour for the month of October.

2134
01:37:45.580 --> 01:37:46.080
Amazing.

2135
01:37:46.320 --> 01:37:48.820
We're going to put all of your tour dates in our Instagram.

2136
01:37:48.820 --> 01:37:49.500
Oh, thank you.

2137
01:37:49.600 --> 01:37:49.840
Yes.

2138
01:37:50.000 --> 01:37:50.400
Thank you.

2139
01:37:50.580 --> 01:37:53.440
And then we're so thrilled because you are here today.

2140
01:37:53.740 --> 01:37:57.480
This was actually something Jenna and I have talked about for years, and then you brought

2141
01:37:57.480 --> 01:37:59.080
it back up to us, Creed.

2142
01:37:59.160 --> 01:38:00.440
But I called it accidentally that time.

2143
01:38:01.080 --> 01:38:04.600
And will you tell everybody you really have called accidentally?

2144
01:38:04.860 --> 01:38:07.280
You know, online, people think that we set that up.

2145
01:38:07.280 --> 01:38:08.100
No, no folks.

2146
01:38:08.100 --> 01:38:09.200
No, you really just called.

2147
01:38:09.220 --> 01:38:09.760
Fans of the office, ladies.

2148
01:38:10.040 --> 01:38:14.820
I just called to check in because I was curious to see where you guys were on the show.

2149
01:38:14.920 --> 01:38:17.100
And I thought, you know, I'll call Pumpkin and check in.

2150
01:38:17.380 --> 01:38:18.180
And you did.

2151
01:38:18.280 --> 01:38:18.860
And I did.

2152
01:38:18.960 --> 01:38:20.120
And then you guys were on the air.

2153
01:38:20.320 --> 01:38:21.680
So no, that's honest to God.

2154
01:38:21.840 --> 01:38:25.000
And I know Creed lies, but myself as Creed, I don't lie.

2155
01:38:25.120 --> 01:38:25.760
That's true.

2156
01:38:25.940 --> 01:38:26.700
That the character does.

2157
01:38:26.900 --> 01:38:30.900
Well, this song is one that you sang on the finale.

2158
01:38:31.320 --> 01:38:31.980
That's right.

2159
01:38:37.280 --> 01:38:41.540
I'm in, it's probably about, I don't know, how long was it before we did the table read?

2160
01:38:41.600 --> 01:38:45.880
You know, before we did the table read, a month and a half, a month, a month, at least

2161
01:38:45.880 --> 01:38:46.560
over a month.

2162
01:38:47.320 --> 01:38:53.320
So I'm in my trailer, and we've all been talking, how are we going to possibly end this

2163
01:38:53.320 --> 01:38:55.460
show, this amazing show that we all love?

2164
01:38:55.680 --> 01:38:57.140
What are we going to do for the finale?

2165
01:38:57.280 --> 01:38:58.340
It's got to be amazing.

2166
01:38:58.760 --> 01:39:03.420
Now, Greg Daniels came back to right the ship and do it with us, you know?

2167
01:39:03.880 --> 01:39:06.860
So I'm sitting in my trailer, and there's a knock on the door, and it's a PA.

2168
01:39:07.820 --> 01:39:10.700
Now, you know, Raina and I have trained them never to look us in the eye.

2169
01:39:11.020 --> 01:39:11.580
Stop it.

2170
01:39:11.600 --> 01:39:12.080
No, don't.

2171
01:39:12.260 --> 01:39:13.260
I opened the door.

2172
01:39:13.780 --> 01:39:14.940
To the production assistant.

2173
01:39:15.160 --> 01:39:17.280
His head production assistant, they help us out on the show.

2174
01:39:17.440 --> 01:39:18.200
So his eyes are down.

2175
01:39:18.300 --> 01:39:19.480
He goes, oh, Mr. Bratton.

2176
01:39:19.480 --> 01:39:20.340
I said, speak up.

2177
01:39:20.500 --> 01:39:21.720
And he went, oh, Mr. Bratton.

2178
01:39:21.760 --> 01:39:22.600
I said, not so loud.

2179
01:39:23.620 --> 01:39:25.600
And so he, I said, what do you want?

2180
01:39:25.660 --> 01:39:27.740
He said, Gray wants to see you in his office.

2181
01:39:27.860 --> 01:39:28.820
I said, why didn't you say so?

2182
01:39:29.040 --> 01:39:30.300
So I push him out of the way.

2183
01:39:30.420 --> 01:39:30.880
I stopped it.

2184
01:39:30.880 --> 01:39:33.400
And I charge, I charge, what's up, boss?

2185
01:39:33.720 --> 01:39:34.740
I always said that with Gray.

2186
01:39:34.840 --> 01:39:35.460
What's up, boss?

2187
01:39:35.780 --> 01:39:36.520
I said, oh, Creed.

2188
01:39:36.520 --> 01:39:37.280
Creed, ah, Creed.

2189
01:39:37.700 --> 01:39:41.440
I'm asking all the actors how you think your character should lead the show.

2190
01:39:42.500 --> 01:39:47.380
So I said, well, I wrote this song called All the Faces in 1970, right after I left the

2191
01:39:47.380 --> 01:39:47.920
grassroots.

2192
01:39:48.280 --> 01:39:50.220
I'm sitting in my house in Ramirez Canyon.

2193
01:39:51.080 --> 01:39:55.860
My wife is in the other room, and my daughter, Ami, is in their little bassinet, and I'm playing

2194
01:39:55.860 --> 01:39:56.780
guitar by the fire.

2195
01:39:57.180 --> 01:39:58.100
And she yells at me.

2196
01:39:58.280 --> 01:39:59.880
She said, that's a beautiful song.

2197
01:40:00.000 --> 01:40:00.480
Who wrote that?

2198
01:40:00.540 --> 01:40:01.900
And I said, I think I just did.

2199
01:40:01.900 --> 01:40:03.700
So I told Greg this.

2200
01:40:03.900 --> 01:40:04.880
He said, well, let me hear it.

2201
01:40:05.060 --> 01:40:09.820
And I said, I think I should be playing this song in Poor Richard's and all the cast, all

2202
01:40:09.820 --> 01:40:10.960
you guys walk through.

2203
01:40:11.120 --> 01:40:13.300
We see your faces, and I'm singing this song.

2204
01:40:13.900 --> 01:40:15.020
He hears the song.

2205
01:40:15.200 --> 01:40:16.300
I can see he's moved.

2206
01:40:17.400 --> 01:40:19.480
I don't hear another word.

2207
01:40:20.100 --> 01:40:21.740
Cut to a month and a half later.

2208
01:40:21.740 --> 01:40:22.640
We get on a bus.

2209
01:40:22.940 --> 01:40:25.220
We go over to Universal, right?

2210
01:40:25.960 --> 01:40:26.440
Everybody's there.

2211
01:40:26.520 --> 01:40:29.880
The brass NBC and Universal and the photographers and the press.

2212
01:40:30.200 --> 01:40:31.840
Big finale table read.

2213
01:40:32.080 --> 01:40:32.400
Big deal.

2214
01:40:32.720 --> 01:40:32.880
Yeah.

2215
01:40:33.200 --> 01:40:36.440
And we're reading the finale, and we're going through with our yellow markers, marking where

2216
01:40:36.440 --> 01:40:37.060
we're going to talk.

2217
01:40:37.480 --> 01:40:41.080
And I just have this little bit at the end, and I come and turn the page over and it says,

2218
01:40:41.260 --> 01:40:43.720
Creed sings his original song, All the Faces.

2219
01:40:44.600 --> 01:40:45.760
That's how you found out.

2220
01:40:45.760 --> 01:40:46.700
That's how I found out.

2221
01:40:46.840 --> 01:40:50.040
At the table read, it's the first time I knew I was going to get to it.

2222
01:40:50.040 --> 01:40:53.540
Because I thought, nah, I tried, but it's not happening.

2223
01:40:53.960 --> 01:40:56.580
And then there was what's happening, and I almost cried.

2224
01:40:57.080 --> 01:40:58.840
And I looked around, and then I started panicking.

2225
01:40:59.000 --> 01:41:00.100
I thought, oh my God, I don't have my guitar.

2226
01:41:00.760 --> 01:41:03.280
And there's that PA that I gave a bad time to.

2227
01:41:03.360 --> 01:41:06.840
He looks, he hands my guitar, but he looks like he's going to drop it, messing with me,

2228
01:41:06.900 --> 01:41:07.020
you know.

2229
01:41:07.540 --> 01:41:08.600
Payback's a bitch, folks.

2230
01:41:09.400 --> 01:41:12.200
So Greg had arranged for your guitar to be there?

2231
01:41:12.200 --> 01:41:12.600
Yes, yes.

2232
01:41:12.620 --> 01:41:13.400
Oh my gosh.

2233
01:41:13.760 --> 01:41:14.620
And I sang it.

2234
01:41:15.400 --> 01:41:19.420
And of course, and the executives are there, and there's not a dry eye in the house.

2235
01:41:19.420 --> 01:41:20.140
It's not at all.

2236
01:41:20.320 --> 01:41:23.440
And by the way, we know these people eat their own, for God's sake.

2237
01:41:24.060 --> 01:41:26.240
You even made the execs cry, Creed.

2238
01:41:26.240 --> 01:41:27.000
I made the execs cry.

2239
01:41:27.260 --> 01:41:28.580
So that's the story.

2240
01:41:28.780 --> 01:41:29.720
So then I played it.

2241
01:41:29.920 --> 01:41:30.720
One more story.

2242
01:41:30.900 --> 01:41:35.500
When we were recording it, Brian couldn't get the boom right, because it was in the shot.

2243
01:41:35.980 --> 01:41:39.360
And John Krasinski says, he's sitting next to you.

2244
01:41:39.500 --> 01:41:39.720
Yeah.

2245
01:41:39.880 --> 01:41:43.440
And he says, Creed, I'll put the microphone under my arm.

2246
01:41:43.980 --> 01:41:48.380
So he puts this long telescopic shotgun mic underneath his arm right out here.

2247
01:41:48.400 --> 01:41:49.680
So it's picking up my guitar.

2248
01:41:50.220 --> 01:41:52.940
So thank you, John, for recording my guitar.

2249
01:41:53.620 --> 01:41:53.860
Yeah.

2250
01:41:54.180 --> 01:41:57.180
What was that like for you playing for us in that scene?

2251
01:41:57.400 --> 01:41:59.720
I mean, it was very emotional for us.

2252
01:41:59.720 --> 01:42:01.160
It was emotional for me, too.

2253
01:42:01.160 --> 01:42:06.660
I had to just tie it together and get real professional, because I could have broken up.

2254
01:42:06.800 --> 01:42:08.720
But I just, all it was, I was just, I'm in my head.

2255
01:42:08.800 --> 01:42:09.560
I'm not paying any attention.

2256
01:42:09.720 --> 01:42:11.240
I'm just singing the song.

2257
01:42:11.540 --> 01:42:11.860
Right.

2258
01:42:12.120 --> 01:42:12.840
Well, we-

2259
01:42:12.840 --> 01:42:13.560
